# Testing And Documentation

- Write meaningful tests that assert behavior, not implementation trivia.
- Cover employee CRUD, validation failures, not-found cases, salary insights, and transaction rollback where useful.
- Use deterministic fixtures and seed data so tests are fast and repeatable.
- Keep test database setup separate from local development data.
- Add frontend tests only where they improve confidence in key user flows.
- Update documentation when setup commands, migrations, seed behavior, APIs, or architecture decisions change.
- Include commands for backend setup, frontend setup, migrations, seeding, tests, and running the app.
- Keep architecture and trade-off notes concise enough for assessment reviewers to scan.
- Include AI usage notes that explain how AI helped and how correctness was verified.
